            "review_text": "DerekChong\nSingapore, Singapore19 contributions\n0\nFantastic herbal duck noodle is Ho Chi Minh\nJul 2016\nA little noodle restaurant in district 5. Traditional setting and it's family owned and run for 3 generations. I was very reluctant to write about this restaurant as I was worried that I will have to wait in a long queue after this is published.\n\nI spoke with the owner of the restaurant, their noodle is home made and the formula for the herbal soup is a secret. I ordered the Mushroom and Duck Noodle and the noodle has a nice texture. The portion of duck is big, It's almost like a quarter of the duck. We ordered fried Wanton and Wanton Soup too with fresh soya milk drink. 6 of us spent about 880K dong.\nRead more\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten July 18, 2016",
            "rating": 5.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-14",
            "travel_date": "Recent",
