            "review_text": "Ararielle\nWarsaw, Poland647 contributions\n0\nWow - amazing duck and fried wontons!\nOct 2015 • Friends\nWe were looking for a good place to eat in Saigon's Chinatown (Cholon) and I found this place as recommended on someone's blog. We went there by Uber, but it turned out that at the given address there was no restaurant. Luckily, our friend had maps on his phone working offline, so we used them to track down the place by its name (it was around a kilometre away). Lot's of locals, which is always a good sign:) We ordered the duck in broth and fried wontons... and WOW, they were both Great! The service was super friendly (it looks like a family-run business, the waiter told us they've had the restaurant for 40 years). This is a must if you visit Chinatown! 5 stars:)\nRead more\nWritten October 25, 2015",
